   128	billing ceiling.
   129	
   130	**Launcher handoff (draft 5).** The launcher copy pushes to the pod, before every paid driver call, its current
   131	`<name>.attempts` file and the ledger, and passes `--attempts`, `--ledger`, `--run-tag`, `--started-at` (the current pod's
   132	allocation time), `--usd-per-hour` (the price ceiling MAXCPH), `--stop-file /root/STOP`, and `--soft-deadline` (its soft
   133	deadline). The driver reads the launcher's own event lines (`<pod> <epoch> start`, `<pod> <epoch> deleted`;
   134	`guards.attempts_spend`): each closed attempt counts at the ceiling, the open start is the current pod (counted from
   135	`--started-at`), and malformed or unordered lines are refused (tests with lines in the launcher's exact format); spend of
   136	earlier launches comes from the ledger rows tagged with the run tag, since the launcher truncates its file per launch. The
   137	driver checks the STOP file and the soft deadline before each internal stage or round, so a single `--stage all` call
   138	honours the launcher's between-stage stop (test).
   139	
   140	**Launcher and the cap.** The pod launcher is a copy of `results/pods/reset_pod.sh` with `results/pods/podctl.py`. Its soft
   141	deadline is the cap at the price ceiling MAXCPH, counted from the first creation request of the launch, so it holds across
   142	attempts; at the soft deadline the remote script stops before its next stage (a STOP file read between stages), and the
   143	driver's own admission check (`--cap-usd`, `--started-at`, `--attempts`) stops between stages or rounds as well. A running
   144	stage is never stopped (the author: do not kill jobs). The single exception is the watchdog, which deletes the pod at 1.3 x
   145	the cap at the price ceiling; that is the only mid-stage stop. Closed attempts are listed in the launcher's
   146	`<name>.attempts` file (pod, start, end, price), which the driver reads (`guards.prior_from_attempts`) and counts toward the
   147	cap before each paid attempt; a paid run without it is refused (no default of zero); after the launch the spend is recorded
   148	in the ledger (`budget_v2.py --record`).
   149	
   150	## 7. Steps
   151	
   152	1. Internal review to consensus; freeze the plan; save the Mac gate evidence.
   153	2. Reserve 4.25 USD in the ledger; one pod: the gate with `--site pod`, then `convergence_v2.py --workers 16 --evidence
   154	   <four gate records> --cap-usd 4.25 --started-at T --attempts A --ledger L --run-tag convergence --stop-file /root/STOP --soft-deadline S`; delete and verify; record the spend.
   155	3. Analysis on the Mac; a paper sentence and table, exploratory, after review.
